  (text "82077AA floppy controller $C030 (FDC_CS from the 74HC138): A0-A2 select its eight\nregisters.  PC/AT mode (IDENT high, MFM open), as on the 65-16.  No DMA: /DACK high,\nTC low; use non-DMA mode (SPECIFY ND=1) and poll the main status register or\ntake the interrupt.  INT and DRQ are tristated until DOR bit 3 is set, so set it.\nINT goes to VIA CB2.  RESET (active high) is NOT RESB, from the CPLD.\n/INVERT low: the chip drives the cable directly (40 mA outputs); 1k pull-ups on\nthe five drive inputs.  J FLOPPY is the PC 34-pin pinout, odd pins ground; with\na twisted PC cable the drive after the twist is drive 0 (DS0/ME0).\nDENSEL jumper: 1-2 controller DENSEL to pin 2, 2-3 pin 2 low.  3.5\" drives\nmostly ignore pin 2 (720K and 1.44M sense the disk).  Drive power: J FDD_POWER,\n1 +5V, 2-3 GND, 4 (+12 V) not connected; a 3.5\" drive needs only 5 V.\n24 MHz crystal: 500/250 kbit/s data rates." (at 25.4 227.97 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 9aeb473b-e1f8-4af0-b58f-9fbc8c68845b)
  )
)
